  <!-- ST HELENS HOUSING STOCK - UNIQUE SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">LOCAL EXPERTISE</span>
      <h2>St Helens Housing. What Our Engineers Find.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">St Helens has a distinct mix of homes built across five different eras, each with its own plumbing quirks. Our engineers have worked on hundreds of St Helens homes and know what to expect before they arrive.</p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.5rem;margin-top:2rem;">

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">WA10</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Town Centre and the Pilkington Terraces</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">The dense terraced streets of WA10 were built for Pilkington Glass workers and the wider industrial workforce in the late 1800s and early 1900s. These homes share traits with their Liverpool cousins: gravity-fed hot water from cold tanks in the loft, original or once-swapped copper pipework, and drain layouts built for a different era. Many WA10 terraces have been split into HMOs over the decades, and these multi-let homes can throw up tricky faults where a problem in one flat hits water supply to several others. We handle HMO call-outs across WA10 often and know the extra complexity they bring.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">WA11</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Haydock and Rainford</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Haydock is mostly post-war semi and detached housing, much of it built between the 1950s and 1970s. Homes of this era used copper pipework that is now reaching the end of its design life in many cases. Boilers in these homes are often the original 1970s and 1980s back boilers or early combi units that have outlived their working life. Rainford by contrast has a mix of older village homes and newer private estates. We work on Haydock and Rainford often and carry stock for the most common faults found in this era of housing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">WA12</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Newton-le-Willows and Earlestown</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Newton-le-Willows is a market town with a varied home mix. The streets around Earlestown station hold Victorian and Edwardian terraces with older plumbing layouts. The outskirts of Newton have large private estates built from the 1980s onwards with modern combi boilers. The M6 corridor around Newton has also seen big growth in business and logistics sites, and we cover 24/7 commercial plumbing across WA12 at the same fixed rates as our home service. Newton also has more buy-to-let homes than much of St Helens borough, and we work with landlords and letting agents across WA12 to keep gas safety up to date.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">WA9 WN5</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Thatto Heath, Billinge and Surrounding Villages</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">The villages around St Helens town, including Billinge, Seneley Green and Thatto Heath, have a mix of older cottage homes and 1960s to 1980s local authority housing. The former mining areas here have older heating that predates the spread of combi boilers. Many homes still run vented hot water cylinders and older heating set-ups that need an engineer who knows how they work. Billinge in particular sits on the boundary with Wigan borough and the housing stock here shows that split between the two areas.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- COMMON JOBS -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f8fafc;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Common Emergencies We Fix Across St Helens</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">The plumbing faults we attend most often across WA10, WA11, WA12 and surrounding areas.</p>
      <div class="jobs-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Burst Pipes and Water Through the Ceiling</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">£120 to £350</span><span class="job-time">30 to 90 mins</span></div><p>Common in WA10 Victorian terraces where loft tanks and outdoor pipework have never been insulated. We stop the leak, repair or swap the bad section and check for hidden water damage before we leave your St Helens home.</p></div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>No Hot Water and Boiler Breakdown</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">£150 to £500</span><span class="job-time">45 to 120 mins</span></div><p>From old back boilers in WA10 terraces to modern condensing units in Newton-le-Willows, we diagnose and repair on the same visit. Most St Helens boiler call-outs are sorted on the first visit with parts from the van. Gas Safe engineers only.</p></div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Blocked Toilets and Drains</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">£80 to £250</span><span class="job-time">30 to 90 mins</span></div><p>Stop flushing and call us. Old clay drainage across WA10 is prone to root ingress and scale. We use proper clearing kit on every drain blockage job. Most St Helens drain blocks are cleared on the same visit.</p></div>
        <div class="job-card job-card--warning"><h3>Gas Leaks</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">FREE safety visit</span><span class="job-time">Priority response</span></div><p>If you smell gas, get out and call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Then call us. Gas safety make-safe visit is FREE. Gas Safe registered engineers only on all gas work across St Helens.</p></div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Major Leaks</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">£80 to £200</span><span class="job-time">20 to 60 mins</span></div><p>Leaking radiators, pipes under sinks, toilet cistern failures and valve issues. We find the source fast and repair or swap the part before it causes water damage. Most major leak call-outs in St Helens are sorted within 60 minutes.</p></div>
        <div class="job-card"><h3>Heating Failure</h3><div class="job-meta"><span class="job-price">£120 to £350</span><span class="job-time">60 to 120 mins</span></div><p>Heating failing is a priority in cold months. We check pump, motor valves, thermostats and pipework on every heating call-out across St Helens. Priority response for elderly and vulnerable people in WA10, WA11 and WA12.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ALL ST HELENS SERVICES -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">All Plumbing and Heating Services Across St Helens</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub" style="text-align:center;">Not an emergency? We cover the full range of plumbing and heating work across WA10, WA11 and WA12.</p>
      <div class="services-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <a href="/boiler-installation-st-helens" class="service-card" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid var(--orange);display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
          <strong style="color:var(--navy);">Boiler Installation St Helens</strong>
