          <p>St Helens has a big share of Victorian and Edwardian terraced housing, especially across WA10. These homes were built with gravity-fed water systems using cold tanks in the loft. In freezing weather, those loft tanks and the pipes feeding them are very prone to freezing and bursting, especially where loft insulation has been added over the top of the tank rather than under it. Our engineers know these systems and know exactly what to look for on a burst pipe call in the older parts of St Helens town.</p>
          <h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;margin:0.75rem 0 0.4rem;text-align:center;">Is ECO4 funding available for St Helens homeowners?</h3>
          <p>Yes. The ECO4 government scheme funds boiler swaps and heating upgrades for eligible homes including those on certain benefits and low income homes. St Helens has a high share of eligible homes across WA10 and WA9. We can check if you qualify and run the application for you as part of a new boiler or central heating fit. See our <a href="/central-heating-installation-st-helens">central heating St Helens page</a> for more detail.</p>
        </div>
